  "clues": {
    "kinetics": "Its food effect is negligible, so it can be taken without regard to food. About 61% to 65% is protein bound, and about 80% of the dose is recovered in urine.",
    "substance": "A crystalline solid, slightly soluble in water, with a molecular weight of 529.5.",
    "product": "Approved under an NDA in 400 mg and 200 mg tablet strengths, plus 150 mg and 200 mg pellets.",
    "safety": "Boxed warning of hepatitis B reactivation, with cases of fulminant hepatitis, hepatic failure and death; its combination partners' contraindications also apply. Fatigue and headache are most common.",
    "indication": "Chronic hepatitis C genotypes 1 to 4 in adults, as part of a combination regimen; children 3 and older with genotype 2 or 3.",
    "mechanism": "A direct-acting antiviral nucleotide analog that inhibits the hepatitis C NS5B polymerase."
  },
  "tell": "A 0.4-hour parent half-life against a 27-hour metabolite sets this hepatitis C drug apart.",
